{
  "title": "Fincept Terminal \u2014 fintech (22,093\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Fincept Terminal\nDomain: fintech | Scale: large | Stars: 22,093\nProblem: Provides institutional-grade financial analytics, market intelligence, and investment research tools to democratize access to professional-level financial data and AI-driven decision-making previously available only to Bloomberg Terminal subscribers.\nTarget users: Retail investors, Professional traders, Investment research analysts, Portfolio managers, Quantitative analysts, Financial institutions\nCore features: Multi-Asset Analytics (DCF models, portfolio optimization, risk metrics); AI Agents framework with 37 specialized agents (Trader/Investor, Economic, Geopolitics); 100+ Data Connectors (Polygon, Kraken, Yahoo Finance, FRED, IMF, World Bank, AkShare); Equity Research and fundamental analysis tools; Portfolio management and tracking; Financial news aggregation and market intelligence; Node Editor for custom workflow automation; Algorithmic trading capabilities\nIntegrations: OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, Groq, DeepSeek, MiniMax, OpenRouter, Ollama, Polygon, Kraken, Yahoo Finance, FRED, IMF, World Bank, DBnomics, AkShare\nTech stack: Qt6 (C++20 native desktop UI) + C++20 core engine with embedded Python + Desktop native binary with multi-provider LLM connectivity\nKey libraries: Qt6, C++20, Python 3.11+, CMake, Multiple LLM providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Groq, DeepSeek, Ollama)\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Hybrid C++/Python architecture leverages native performance (C++20) for core engine with Python embedded for analytics and ML flexibility\n- Multi-provider LLM abstraction layer enables vendor-agnostic AI agents with 37 specialized personas across trading, economics, and geopolitics domains\n- 100+ data connector strategy eliminates vendor lock-in and democratizes access to institutional-grade market data sources\n- Desktop-first native application (Qt6) prioritizes performance and reliability over web-based deployment for professional trading workflows",
